---Refresh table schema from source
---
---Re-introspect an existing direct-read warehouse table's schema from its underlying source files and overwrite its stored column list. Use when the source schema has evolved (e.g. new columns in the underlying Delta/Parquet/CSV files) but queries still can't see the new columns, because PostHog serves a cached column snapshot until the table is refreshed. This applies only to existing direct-read tables. New direct-read tables cannot be created. Tables managed by an external data source sync refresh on their own schedule.
---
---`POST /api/projects/{project_id}/warehouse_tables/{id}/refresh_schema/`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input posthog.warehouse_tables.WarehouseTablesRefreshSchemaCreateRequest
---@return posthog.warehouse_tables.WarehouseTablesRefreshSchemaCreateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:warehouse_tables_refresh_schema_create(input) end

---Replace the file of a table made from an uploaded file
---
---Point a table made from an uploaded file at a new upload, then import it with one full refresh. Upload the new file with upload_file first. The table keeps its id and its name, and its rows are replaced when the sync finishes. The old file is deleted only after that sync succeeds. The sync bills its rows like any other import.
---
---`POST /api/projects/{project_id}/warehouse_tables/{id}/replace_file/`
---@param input posthog.warehouse_tables.WarehouseTablesReplaceFileCreateRequest
---@return posthog.warehouse_tables.WarehouseTablesReplaceFileCreateResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:warehouse_tables_replace_file_create(input) end

